(Startup Language Documentation) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Specification and examples for the .startup DSL compiler playground.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(1. Language Purpose) Tj
0 -14 Td
(.startup is a compact educational DSL designed to make core compiler stages visible:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(lexing, parsing, semantic analysis, IR generation, and runtime execution.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(2. Core Rules) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Every statement ends with ? \(parser can recover if omitted in some cases\).) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Blocks use [ and ], and conditions use \( and \).) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Line comments start with // and continue to the end of line.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Strings use double quotes, for example Vibe name ::> "Nova"?.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Booleans are written as VESTED \(true\) and CLIFF \(false\).) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Naming convention: variables in camelCase, classes in PascalCase.) Tj
0 -14 Td
